{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>Bless</b> — [the meaning of] ha-amim is 'the peoples,' like the Jebusites who were under Israel's hand. Or he says to all of us — we are all obligated to bless HaShem." "And some say: the meaning of amim is Israel, as in 'after you, Benjamin, among your peoples' (1 Samuel 5:12 [var.]), and this is the correct interpretation."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 66, :notes {1 "Ibn Ezra's citation 'אחריך בנימן בעממיך' does not correspond to any standard verse reference; rendered hyper-literally as quoted."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:32:52.419722891Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}